  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Hive of Silent is a game developed as part of an assignment for Raion
    Community, created with the primary goal of recreating and understanding the
    core gameplay mechanics of Hollow Knight. This project serves as both a technical
    exploration and a practical implementation of game development principles, focusing
    on how a well-designed system can deliver responsive controls, engaging combat,
    and structured enemy encounters. The recreated mechanics include a fluid movement
    system that emphasizes player control and responsiveness, a combat system that
    incorporates timing and interaction, and a boss phase system that demonstrates
    dynamic behavior changes during encounters.


    Beyond replicating gameplay
    features, the development of this game also highlights the application of object-oriented
    programming concepts in a real-world scenario. The system architecture leverages
    inheritance to promote code reuse, polymorphism to enable flexible behavior implementation,
    and interfaces to define clear contracts between components. Additionally, event
    and action systems are utilized to handle interactions and communication between
    different parts of the game, ensuring modularity and scalability. Through this
    approach, the project not only recreates gameplay mechanics but also demonstrates
    how structured programming techniques can support the development of complex
    interactive systems.


    This project represents a combination of technical
    practice and creative execution, aiming to deepen the understanding of both game
    design and software engineering principles by rebuilding and analyzing the mechanics
    of an established game.


    Game Programmer

    Aditya Rajadana Hernadi


    Game
    Artist

    Aditya Rajadana Hernadi


    Background Assets

    Google'
